<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - April 4.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - April 4.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 04/04/97  03/28/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     10.78     10.26     4.64	 4.41	2.3</p>
<p>West	     46.61     44.92    17.99	17.34     26.8</p>
<p>Total Canada   57.39     55.19    11.67	11.22     15.2</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 04/04/97: 232.55 bcf, 03/28/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 04/04/97: 259.11 bcf, 03/28/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
